##RenderMan RIB-Structure 1.0
# A static point carries the extra output (an AOV, here P, in the space the points are given in) of its own vertex.
# Two points on the image row 32: the channel P.y reads 0.5 over both discs (the discs are about 12 pixels wide, the test reads 9 of them).
version 3.03
Hider "reyes"
Option "shaderformat" "default" ["rslo"]
PixelSamples 1 1
PixelFilter "box" 1 1
Quantize "rgba" 0 0 0 0
Display "shading-interpolation-aov-points-reyes-rgba.tif" "file" "rgba"
Display "+shading-interpolation-aov-points-reyes.tif" "file" "P"
Projection "orthographic"
ScreenWindow 0 1 0 1
Format 64 64 1
Clipping 0.1 100
Translate 0 0 1
WorldBegin
  Surface "constant"
  Points "P" [0.25 0.5 0  0.75 0.5 0] "constantwidth" [0.2]
WorldEnd
